1 LOGOUT

   Ends a process's DCL and the process: a subprocess's, a batch job's,
   or, in the console's own process, govax.

   Format

     LOGOUT

2 Description

   The process says so, and its final status is $STATUS's.  A spawned
   subprocess writes "Process name logged out at ...".  A login (an
   interactive process, or the console's own) writes "username logged
   out at ...", and a batch job "username job terminated at ...",
   followed in its log by the accounting information: the process's I/O
   counts, page faults, peak working set and page file sizes, CPU time,
   and elapsed time.  /BRIEF and /FULL choose the short and long forms;
   an interactive process's default is /BRIEF, any other's /FULL.  They
   are one setting: /NOFULL is /BRIEF and /NOBRIEF is /FULL, and if both
   are given the last one counts, so after LO*GOUT := LOGOUT/FULL the
   command LO/BRIEF writes the short form.

   In the console's own process LOGOUT ends govax, from the terminal or
   from inside a command procedure: the report is written, mounted
   volumes are dismounted, and the other processes deleted.  EXIT at the
   terminal ends govax with no report.  LO is LOGOUT, though other
   verbs begin with it.  See SPAWN.

2 Qualifiers

/BRIEF

      /BRIEF
      /NOBRIEF

   Writes only the line that says the process logged out.  The default
   for an interactive process.  /NOBRIEF is /FULL.

/FULL

      /FULL
      /NOFULL

   Writes the accounting information after that line.  The default for
   a process that isn't interactive, such as a batch job.  /NOFULL is
   /BRIEF.

2 Examples

   1.$ LOGOUT
       SYSTEM       logged out at 16-NOV-2026 17:11:24.07

   2.$ LOGOUT/FULL
       SYSTEM       logged out at 16-NOV-2026 17:02:56.40

       Accounting information:
       Buffered I/O count:             121         Peak working set size:     662
       Direct I/O count:                50         Peak page file size:      4493
       Page faults:                   1700         Mounted volumes:             0
       Charged CPU time:           0 00:00:00.05   Elapsed time:     0 00:00:44.20
